From 0c5d83b1bc2c6f2734c995915eecea94b90c9461 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 00:10:12 +0000
Subject: cranelift/pulley: fuse band+brif at call_indirect lazy-init site
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wires the new Pulley xband_s8 + br_if fused ops (previous commit) into
the Cranelift Pulley backend. At call_indirect lazy-init brif sites
under the is_eagerly_initialized_funcref_table predicate, the band-imm +
brif pair now lowers to a single Pulley dispatch instead of two — the
smallest measurable step past PR #2's c1-7 predictor-anchor ceiling on
the "next branch -- opcode fusion" track.

Layered changes:

  func_environ: when is_eagerly_initialized_funcref_table holds, the
  call_indirect brif tests value_masked (the band's result) instead of
  the unmasked loaded funcref. This is semantically equivalent on every
  reachable slot value in eagerly-initialized tables: the only diverging
  case is the explicit tagged-null slot value 1 (produced by
  table.fill(null) on a tagged table), which the immutability half of
  the predicate excludes. The rewrite unlocks the ISLE pattern match.

  pulley_shared::inst: new MInst::BandBrIf terminator variant carrying
  dst, src, mask, size (32/64), and the two branch targets. Treated as
  a Branch by is_term; the operand collector reports dst as a def and
  src as a use, so regalloc allocates the band-result vreg the same way
  as a standalone xband_s8 would.

  pulley_shared::lower::try_fuse_band_brif: Rust-side pre-ISLE peephole
  in lower_branch. Recognizes brif(c) where c = band(v, -2) — restricted
  to exactly the funcref init-bit-strip mask — and emits BandBrIf with
  dst = the brif-cond's vreg (i.e. the band's result vreg). The band
  CLIF inst is then marked via Lower::sink_pure_inst so it is skipped
  in lower_clif_block, leaving a single MachInst writing to the
  band-result vreg. The block-call-arg machinery downstream consumes
  that vreg as the masked-funcref pointer with no SSA violation.

  The mask = -2 gate is load-bearing: the fused op tests the UNMASKED
  src for non-zero, not the masked dst. That equivalence holds iff
  (v & mask != 0) <=> (v != 0). For mask = -2 this holds on every
  reachable funcref-slot value under the eager-init predicate; for
  other i8 masks (e.g. user-code band(v, 127) or band(v, 60)) the
  equivalence fails and fusing would silently flip branch direction.
  Restricting to mask = -2 keeps the lowering sound by construction.

  pulley_shared::inst::emit: BandBrIf emits as the forward
  xband_s8_br_if op followed by an unconditional jump to not_taken,
  with the inverted xband_s8_br_if_not op encoded into the
  add_cond_branch slot so MachBuffer can flip branch direction for
  fallthrough optimization. Same encoding scaffolding as Inst::BrIf.

Tests:

  tests/disas/call-indirect-immutable-elide-null.wat: blessed CLIF
  diff — brif now reads v13 (the masked value) instead of v12 (the
  loaded value) when the predicate holds.

  tests/disas/pulley-call-indirect-band-brif-fusion.wat: new pulley64
  disas test pinning the fused-op bytecode shape. The dispatch tail
  shows a single xband64_s8_br_if_not_x64 where the unfused form would
  have an xband64_s8 followed by a separate br_if_xeq64_i8.
